Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.56,0:00:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.68,0:00:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Dr. Michael Clarkson.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.83,0:00:07.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome to Functional Programming in OCaml.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.36,0:00:10.11,Default,,0,0,0,,My main job is teaching university students\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.11,0:00:15.08,Default,,0,0,0,,to write correct, efficient, and beautiful programs.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.08,0:00:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,In the last few years, I've taught OCaml\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.55,0:00:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,to about 3,700 students at Cornell University\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.07,0:00:25.80,Default,,0,0,0,,in a course titled CS3110, Data Structures\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.80,0:00:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,and Functional Programming.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.51,0:00:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You might have come across this video in any number of ways.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.15,0:00:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you're actually a student in CS 3110 right now.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.25,0:00:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you're not a Cornell student,\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.75,0:00:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,but you're looking to learn something\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.25,0:00:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,about functional programming.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.28,0:00:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you came here from the online textbook\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.37,0:00:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,in which this video is embedded, or maybe you\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.67,0:00:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,found the video first.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.06,0:00:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,In which case, check the comments below\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.03,0:00:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,for the current link to the textbook.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.92,0:00:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been writing the textbook for a few years now.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.37,0:00:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's based on course notes written by myself\N
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.92,0:01:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,other faculty for over two decades. Beyond teaching functional programming, our goal\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.71,0:01:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,has long been to teach students to be great programmers, to equip them with the knowledge,\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.20,0:01:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,skills, and habits they need to be successful beyond the basics of the usual introductory\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.79,0:01:23.24,Default,,0,0,0,,computer science classes. These videos, however, are new. They came about because of pandemic.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.51,0:01:30.84,Default,,0,0,0,,In the 2020 through 2021 academic year, I taught an asynchronous version of my class.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.64,0:01:38.92,Default,,0,0,0,,That meant these videos had to replace the usual in-person lectures. So I ended up producing over\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.92,0:01:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,200 short videos, most around five to six minutes in length. And the reaction from students was\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.03,0:01:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,overwhelmingly positive. So now I'm making the videos publicly available for anyone who wants\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.31,0:01:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,to learn something about OCaml, functional programming, and becoming a better programmer.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.63,0:02:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you find them useful, maybe even entertaining. They are a love letter for me\N
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.19,0:02:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,to all the students who endured through the time of Zoom U. We did it together. And now,\N
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.35,0:02:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,maybe the world can be just a bit better as we spread the light of functional programming.\N
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.59,0:02:25.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N
